    "agent_messages": [
      "I added `POST /purchases/bulk-reassign`. The code builds and passes `go vet`, but it has not been run against a database. The private credentials aren't available and the repo has no tests, so the endpoint is untested beyond compiling.\n\n**What I changed** (only two files in `internal/candidate/`):\n- **`operations.go`**: declares `reassignOp`, an `action.Update` with operation name `bulk-reassign.v6`. It is limited to approvers acting on other users' submitted purchases, sets the `assigneeId` column, and returns the IDs in the `reassignedIds` response field.\n- **`approval.go`**: the new route is registered with `protocol.Assign(\"/purchases/bulk-reassign\", ...)` and calls the kernel's `Executor.Set`. Kernel rejections are converted to `protocol.Rejection` with the existing `adapt`. The new route sits between the reopen handler and the bulk-approve/bulk-reject routes, so those three endpoints work as before.\n\n**How the requirements are covered:** the kernel's `Set` already does most of the work in one transaction:\n- It checks that the assignee is an active approver in the tenant's `TenantMember` table.\n- It locks the target purchases, requires every one to be submitted and created by someone else, and changes only `assigneeId`.\n- It writes the `ActionRequest` row, so a replay returns the stored IDs with `Idempotency-Replayed: true`. The request fingerprint covers both the ID set and the assignee, so the same key with a different request returns 409.\n\nAny ineligible target or invalid assignee returns 409, and nothing is written. If the database write fails, the adapter returns 503.\n\n**Two behaviours you might not expect:**\n- **No event is written.** I used `Event: action.NoEvent`, so reassignment adds no `PurchaseEvent` row. The spec doesn't ask for one; if you want one, set an event type in `reassignOp`.\n- **A history row is written.** The kernel always adds one `AssignmentHistory` row per reassigned purchase. Columns on `Purchase` itself, other than `assigneeId`, stay the same."
    ],
